            <h2>Built inside Google Chrome and Firefox</h2>
            <p>
                Ui.Vision browser automation runs directly inside the two major browsers. Thus it is fully compatible with any modern website.
                The automation is visual, so there is no new scripting language to learn, you have full programmatic control over the web browser, and even the most complex tasks can be scripted.
            </p>

            <p>
                <em>Ui.Vision RPA</em>'s computer-vision  <a href="/rpa/docs/visual-ui-testing/">codeless UI testing</a> commands
                allow you to write automated visual tests with <em>Ui.Vision RPA</em> - this makes <em>Ui.Vision RPA</em> the first and only Chrome and
                Firefox extension (and Selenium IDE) that has "👁👁 eyes". A huge benefit of doing visual tests is that you are not just checking one element or
                two elements at a time,   you’re checking a whole section or page in one visual assertion.
            </p>

